Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 card album and deck editor fill 16:9

The card album (STCRDABM) and the deck editor (STCRDDEK), both opened from
the field menu's Card folders, ran with gutter 0: a 4:3 picture pillarboxed
on a 16:9 screen. port/options/widescreen.c gives both overlays the menu
gutter and:

- their scrolling background (96 px period) is drawn twice more, 96 pixels to
  each side, as patch 0053;
- the album's title plate hangs from the 16:9 left edge and its "Back" plate
  from the right edge (DW3_MENU_LEFT / DW3_MENU_RIGHT, with their text
  windows and open-animation pivots); the card details at the bottom (kind
  icon, count and points windows, the "x N" plate) are drawn one gutter
  further right and the name and text plates that run off the right edge are
  extended to the picture's edge (DW3_MENU_EXTEND, new in port_widescreen.h);
- the deck editor's title plate is extended the same way, the folder options
  panel (Edit Folder / Change name, its windows and cursor) hangs from the
  right edge, and the editor's right column (the card info panel, the list of
  the cards owned with its lines, cursor and scroll bar, the list card's
  details) follows the album's layout; the folder rows and the 9x5 grid stay
  in the middle 4:3.

Only drawing positions change: the cursors and the pad logic keep their
values. Off (gutter 0) every position is the PS1 one.

